  "interpretation": [
    "Reaction has the clearest small matched-control benefit: primary +0.00895967 dB and second-noise +0.00925521 dB, with 31/32 image improvements on both.",
    "Float64 depth is exploratory: positive same-update curves and mean on both draws, but best-versus-best means are driven by two photographs and image-bootstrap intervals include zero.",
    "Width112 does not beat the matching positive80 control in these bounded pilots; this does not rule out all longer-training width experiments.",
    "Patch100 achieves more updates and receives more checkpoint-selection opportunities under the same time allowance; its selected-best advantage does not isolate patch geometry.",
    "Positive-versus-frozen metric differences are tiny and depend on endpoint/checkpoint choice.",
    "The float32 depth failure is a numerical failure, not a valid zero-gain trained denoiser."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Validation32 is the model-selection set, not BSD68 final test performance.",
    "One training seed; image-bootstrap intervals condition on the selected checkpoints and fixed noise draw and do not estimate training-seed variation.",
    "Best-of-many checkpoints and architecture trials create selection bias; faster runs have more selection opportunities.",
    "Wall-time matching gives unequal completed updates and pixel exposures; common-update comparisons give unequal compute.",
    "Self-control deltas are identically zero by definition and are not independent architecture gains.",
    "Startup, evaluation and failures are included in the reported charged lease; historical checkpoint pretraining and other setup/smoke leases are outside individual pilot charges.",
    "No state-of-the-art, perceptual, global-stability or mobile-performance claim follows from these pilot scores."
